    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "A spacious and beautifully positioned family home, offering generous accommodation, superb living spaces and an exceptional sense of privacy, all set on approximately 0.79 acres of mature grounds in the heart of South Wexford’s countryside. This impressive detached residence combines the peace and privacy of a substantial country site with excellent access to Wexford Town, Kilmore Quay and the many amenities of south-east Wexford. Approached through a mature setting, established trees create a wonderful sense of seclusion and privacy. The property has a distinctive and attractive appearance, with both the residence and front boundary walls finished in natural stone, complementing its rural surroundings. From the moment you enter, the scale and versatility of this home become apparent. At its heart is an impressive open-plan kitchen, living and dining space, designed as a natural hub for family life and entertaining. A large kitchen island provides an excellent focal point, while the generous layout allows distinct kitchen, dining and lounge areas to flow seamlessly together, creating a superb and versatile living environment. A bright sunroom directly off the kitchen provides an additional relaxing space, ideal for enjoying views of the garden and mature surroundings.\r\n\r\nFor more formal entertaining or quieter occasions, the property also benefits from a separate, generously proportion ed sitting room, providing an additional living space away from the main family area. Upstairs, there are four generously proportioned double bedrooms. The principal bedroom benefits from its own  en-suite, providing a private and comfortable retreat. The remaining three bedrooms are all substantial double rooms, offering excellent flexibility and generous personal space. The first floor is completed by a family bathroom  and a useful separate storage room, providing valuable additional storage space that is often lacking in modern homes. Mature trees and established planting provide a high degree of privacy, creating a peaceful country setting\r\nthat is increasingly difficult to find within such convenient reach of Wexford Town and the coast. The property is ideally located just minutes from a host of amenities, including schools, churches, sports clubs, childcare facilities and the renowned Johnstown Castle. Kilmore Quay is also within easy reach and is a picturesque working fishing village, renowned for its harbour, marina and beautiful sandy beaches. The surrounding coastline provides excellent opportunities for walking, swimming, boating and fishing, while Ballyteigue Bay offers spectacular coastal scenery.\r\nWexford Town is approximately 12km away and provides an extensive range of shops, restaurants, cafés, entertainment venues and everyday services."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Accommodation Comprises:\r\nEntrance Hallway – (1.9m x 1.8m),  Tile flooring, alarm system.\r\nHallway – (4.2m x 2.5m),  Tile flooring.\r\nWC – (1.7m x 1.4m),  Tile flooring, WC, WHB, heated towel rail.\r\nKitchen/ Diner/ Lounge – (10.3m x 4.9m),  Tile flooring, Triple aspect, box window, cabinets at waist and eye level, built in oven & 4 ring electric hobs, plumbed for dishwasher, kitchen island, fitted stove, double doors leading to garden.\r\nUtility Room – (3.3m x 2.9m),  Tile flooring, cabinets at waist and eye level, plumbed for washing machine, access to rear garden.\r\nSun Room – (4.1m x 4m),  Tile flooring, double doors to garden.\r\nLiving Room – (7m x 4m),  Carpet flooring, dual aspect, open fire.\r\n\r\nUpstairs\r\n\r\nLanding – (5.7m x 4.2m),  Timber flooring, HP, stira to attic.\r\nBedroom No. 1 – (4.9m x 3.8m),  Timber flooring.\r\nEn Suite – (2.4m x 1.6m),  Tile flooring, half tiled walls, WC, WHB, enclosed shower.\r\nBedroom No. 2 – (4.4m x 3.4m),  Timber flooring, dual aspect.\r\nBedroom No. 3 – (4m x 3.6m),  Timber flooring.\r\nBedroom No. 4 – (4m x 3.3m),  Timber flooring, window to the rear.\r\nBathroom – (2.9m x 2.7m),  Tile flooring, half tiled walls, WC, WHB, bathtub, electric shower\r\nStore Room – (1.6m x 0.8m), Timber flooring.\r\n\r\nOutside: Gravel driveway, spacious parking, gardens to front, side and rear.\r\nServices: Electricity, private water, private sewerage, oil fired central heating.\r\nBER: B Ber No: 108494154 Performance indicator: 140.92 kWh/m2/yr\r\nApply: Keane Auctioneers (053) 9123072"
